MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT

Curriculum Server Central SMS & WhatsApp Infrastructure, Authentication Integration and Reusable School-Instance Communication Feature

1. MISSION AND IMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE

Undertake a comprehensive repository investigation, architecture review, feature development, implementation, integration, testing, and production-readiness exercise to deliver a fully operational, centrally managed SMS and WhatsApp infrastructure for the Curriculum Server ecosystem.

This infrastructure must serve three distinct but interconnected purposes:

1. Curriculum Server platform communications and authentication: SMS and WhatsApp must be available to Curriculum Server itself for platform administration, user authentication, security verification, alerts, notifications, and operational communications.
2. Provisioned school-instance communications and authentication: Every provisioned school instance must be able to use SMS and WhatsApp for its own users, authentication workflows, and school communications.
3. Provisioned Curriculum Flow communications and authentication: Every provisioned Curriculum Flow application must be able to use SMS and WhatsApp for application-level authentication and communications, independently configurable for the institution or tenant it serves.

Do not implement these as disconnected messaging integrations inside individual applications.

Build a centrally governed, reusable, multi-tenant Communication and Messaging Service that can be consumed by Curriculum Server, Curriculum Flow, and all present and future applications provisioned through Curriculum Server.

The implementation must deliver complete feature development, feature registration, application integration, tenant-aware provisioning, operational administration, security, testing, production readiness, and availability through the provisioning system.

This is an implementation assignment, not a proposal or architecture-document-only exercise.

