Build a central service within Curriculum Server called:

Curriculum Messaging & Authentication Gateway (CMAG)

The name may be adapted to existing repository naming conventions, but the architectural responsibilities must remain.

CMAG must provide a common service interface for:

- SMS delivery.
- WhatsApp delivery.
- Authentication OTP delivery.
- Account verification.
- Password recovery.
- MFA and security verification.
- Transactional notifications.
- School announcements.
- Parent and guardian communications.
- Academic notifications.
- Attendance notifications.
- Financial notifications.
- Emergency alerts.
- Administrative notifications.
- Delivery tracking and reporting.

The service must be centrally developed and operated while supporting tenant-specific configurations.

Architectural separation

Implement the following layers:

Layer A — Central Messaging Infrastructure

Responsible for:

- Provider integrations.
- Message dispatch.
- Authentication message dispatch.
- Message templates.
- Queue management.
- Retries and failure handling.
- Delivery receipts.
- Provider health checks.
- Usage accounting.
- Audit logging.
- Rate limiting.
- Security enforcement.
